<title>RUSSIA: Russian VSM bond priced at 94.76 pct, yield 56.48.</title>
<headline>Russian VSM bond priced at 94.76 pct, yield 56.48.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest issue of Russia's RAO Vysokoskorostnye Magistrali (High-Speed Railways or VSM) government-backed bonds were priced at an average 94.76 percent at auction to yield an average 56.48 percent, the Central Bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Series number			RU22VSM0330</p>
<p>    Issue volume			 150 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		     215.69 bln</p>
<p>    Sold				   46.06 bln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			     43.65 bln</p>
<p>    Average price			94.76 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			56.48 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	    94.50 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	   57.73 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor				  365 days</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
